1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,080
Specs, designs and API docs scattered everywhere. AI never gets the full picture.

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:07,880
LoopForgeX puts them on one canvas. You just assign work and make the call.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,480
The whole site is a project map, from intake to shipping. Nothing is hidden.

4
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:18,880
Planning, coding and review go to role-based agents. You only click three times.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,280
The browser opens after install. Three steps on the home page walk you through.

6
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:29,880
Detect an engine, pick a repo, drop your first request. Click a node for details.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,080
Ask the steward, then paste a link, a doc, or words from a product meeting.

8
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:41,880
AI files it into a new cycle. You can just drag files in too.

9
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,080
AI locks the API contract first, then writes the spec, design check and changes.

10
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:53,880
The plan hangs on the node. Open the drawer, review it, then approve.

11
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:00,480
The big calls are yours alone. Approval and kickoff cannot be clicked by AI.

12
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:06,880
One agent per platform in parallel, a second agent reviews independently.

13
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:12,480
The evidence pack shows progress and review results for every requirement.

14
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:17,880
Hit accept: Git pushes a branch, SVN commits only this change.

15
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:22,880
Bugs and crashes sync and group automatically. Designs get checked page by page.

16
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:27,880
Work stats add themselves up, and a steward agent proactively reminds you.

17
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:32,280
Data stays on your own Mac or server. One command to install.

18
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:35,880
Now, put your first request on the canvas.

